  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "criterion": "The Configuration screen displays three tabs: General, Persona Models, Model Registry",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The General tab contains all existing settings (auto_handoff_enabled, max_handoff_depth, capture_dialogues, auto_archive_days, ledger_root) with identical save behavior",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Tab switching re-renders only the tab content area, not the full page",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Switching tabs when unsaved changes exist triggers a confirmation dialog with Discard / Stay options",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Tab CSS uses `.config-tabs` / `.config-tab` class names, visually identical to `.knowledge-tabs` / `.knowledge-tab` styling",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Placeholder stubs exist for Persona Models and Model Registry tabs (display a \"Coming soon\" message or empty state)",
      "met": true
    }
  ],
  "active_pipeline_stages": [
    "implementation",
    "qa",
    "code-review",
    "documentation"
  ],
  "revision": 0,
  "pipelines": [
    {
      "type": "implementation",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-07-21T15:09:42Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-07-21T15:12:19Z",
      "duration_ms": 157000,
      "summary": [
        "Rewrote config.js from a single 79-line renderConfig() function into a tabbed view with module-level state management. Added three tabs: General, Persona Models, Model Registry. Tab switching re-renders only #config-tab-content (not the full page). Unsaved-changes guard uses confirm() with Discard/Stay semantics and resets dirty state on Discard or after a successful save. renderConfig() now loads API.getModels/getPersonas/getAssignments in parallel with API.getConfig() via Promise.all, falling back gracefully when those API methods don't yet exist. Stub tabs for Persona Models and Model Registry render 'Coming soon' empty-state cards. Added .config-tabs / .config-tab CSS to styles.css, mirroring .knowledge-tabs / .knowledge-tab exactly (same flex layout, border-bottom track, margin-bottom overlap, --color-ready active state)."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "mcp-server/gui/public/views/config.js",
          "mcp-server/gui/public/styles.css"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:12:19Z",
          "note": "config.js now uses module-level vars (configActiveTab, configDirty) in the global scope — consistent with the rest of the SPA (e.g. knowledge.js uses a similar pattern). If the SPA grows, consider namespacing these under a ConfigView object to avoid potential global name collisions."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:12:19Z",
          "note": "The dirty-tracking listeners in wireGeneralTabEvents() use both 'change' and 'input' events to cover all input types (checkboxes fire 'change', text inputs fire 'input'). This is intentional and correct, but worth documenting in a comment for the next developer."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:12:19Z",
          "note": "The tab-switch dirty guard uses the native window.confirm() dialog, matching the existing SPA pattern (no custom modal library). If a custom modal system is introduced in future (e.g. for WP-008/009), this should be upgraded to use it for visual consistency."
        },
        {
          "type": "convention",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:12:19Z",
          "note": "styles.css uses a flat append strategy — new view-specific CSS is added to the bottom. The file is now ~3090 lines. A section-based structure (one CSS section per view) would improve navigability; consider a future cleanup pass."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-07-21T15:12:39Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-07-21T15:15:18Z",
      "duration_ms": 159000,
      "summary": [
        "All 6 acceptance criteria verified by static code analysis and runtime regression testing. Full test suite (117 files, 3523 tests) passes with zero regressions. All AC met: three tabs render correctly, General tab contains all five settings with correct save behavior, tab switching only re-renders #config-tab-content, dirty guard uses confirm() with Discard/Stay semantics, .config-tabs/.config-tab CSS is property-for-property identical to .knowledge-tabs/.knowledge-tab, stub tabs display 'Coming soon' messages. One medium-priority UX edge case noted (configDirty persistence after SPA navigation) — not an AC violation, noted as improvement comment."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "test_coverage": "117 test files",
        "tests_passed": 3523,
        "tests_failed": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:15:18Z",
          "note": "configDirty flags (configDirty.general etc.) are never reset on renderConfig() re-entry. Scenario: user makes changes, navigates away WITHOUT saving, then navigates back to config. configDirty.general remains true. Immediately switching tabs triggers the 'You have unsaved changes' dialog spuriously, even though the page just re-fetched fresh config data from the server. Fix: reset all configDirty values to false at the start of renderConfig() or renderConfigPage(). Not an AC violation since WP-007 AC only requires the guard fires when unsaved changes exist within a page session."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:15:18Z",
          "note": "wireGeneralTabEvents() attaches both 'change' and 'input' event listeners to the form. This is intentional (checkboxes fire 'change', text inputs fire 'input'). Consider adding a brief code comment explaining this dual-listener pattern for future developers maintaining the dirty-tracking logic."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:15:18Z",
          "note": "No existing jsdom test suite covers config.js rendering. Future WPs that extend the config view (WP-008, WP-009) may benefit from adding a client-rendering test for config.js using the same vm.runInThisContext pattern used in tests/gui/client-rendering.test.ts."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "status_changed_at": "2026-07-21T15:09:42Z",
  "last_updated": "2026-07-21T15:15:18Z",
  "handoff_notes": [
    {
      "from_agent": "Developer",
      "to_agent": "QA",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:12:19Z",
      "notes": [
        "config.js is now ~200 lines, split into clearly named functions: renderConfig (entry, parallel load), renderConfigPage (scaffold + tab-bar wiring), renderConfigTabContent (dispatcher), renderGeneralTab (HTML), wireGeneralTabEvents (event listeners), renderPersonaModelsTab (stub), renderModelRegistryTab (stub).",
        "Module-level vars configActiveTab and configDirty persist across tab switches within the same page visit. They are intentionally not reset on renderConfig() re-entry — if the page is navigated away from and back, the SPA will call renderConfig(app) again which re-fetches all data and re-renders the scaffold, but configActiveTab will restore to the previously active tab, which is desirable UX.",
        "API.getModels / API.getPersonas / API.getAssignments are guarded with optional-chaining fallbacks (Promise.resolve([])) so the page works now before WP-008/WP-009 add those API methods.",
        "WP-008 (Persona Models tab) and WP-009 (Model Registry tab) should replace the stub return values of renderPersonaModelsTab() and renderModelRegistryTab() respectively — no other function needs to change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:15:18Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 6 AC verified PASS. Full regression suite clean (3523 tests). One medium-priority UX improvement identified: configDirty state persists across SPA navigation — user returning to config page after unsaved-then-abandoned changes will see a spurious dirty dialog. Not blocking for code review, but worth a fix-forward. config.js is clean, well-structured, ~204 lines. CSS mirror is exact. Ready for code review."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

